    "https://foundation.fhsu.edu/about/careers/": {
      "title": "Director of Development",
      "description": "Careers - Fort Hays State University Foundation Ways to Give Give Now Give Online Phone or Mail Stock & Securities Give Over Time Recurring Gifts Pledge Gifts FHSU Faculty & Staff Plan Your Gift Charitable IRA Estate Plan Give Assets Impact Student Stories Donor Impact Campus Capital Projects About Staff News Contact Us Make A Gift Join Our Team Open Positions: Director of Development - College of Education and Tebo Library Posting Date: July 28, 2026 Build Relationships. Inspire Generosity. Transform Futures. Every great university has stories of lives changed through generosity. A scholarship that made college possible. A donor whose vision inspired innovation. Those stories begin with people who believe in connecting passion with purpose. The Fort Hays State University Foundation is seeking a Director of Development to build meaningful relationships with alumni, donors, and friends who want to shape the future of FHSU by investing in two of the university's most transformative areas – the College of Education and the newly renovated Tebo Library . Make an Impact This is more than a fundraising position. As a Director of Development, you'll help the College of Education and Tebo Library by connecting generous supporters with initiatives that align with their passions. Working alongside university leadership, faculty, and Foundation colleagues, you’ll help donors create new scholarships, support essential programs, or advance campus projects. Every conversation has the potential to make a difference, and you’ll see firsthand the tangible results of your work. What You’ll Do Success in this role is built on trust and connection where no two days look alike. One day you'll meet with alumni across Kansas, listening to stories of their time on campus and learning what inspires them to give. The next, you'll collaborate with campus partners to identify fundraising priorities and create ways for donors to make a lasting impact. If you enjoy engaging with people, thinking strategically, and helping others, you'll find this work both rewarding and fulfilling. Who We're Looking For You don't have to come from higher education fundraising to flourish here. If you've built trust, helped clients achieve goals, or connected people with opportunities – whether in business development, sales, financial planning, nonprofit leadership, healthcare, or another relationship-driven field – we'd love to talk with you. The ideal candidate is: Passionate about helping others make a difference. A strong communicator who builds trust naturally. Curious, strategic, and motivated by meaningful work. Comfortable engaging with a wide variety of people and perspectives. Organized and able to manage multiple priorities while maintaining attention to detail. Self-motivated, collaborative, and excited to represent Fort Hays State University. Join Us If you're energized by what you’ve read here, we encourage you to explore the full position description to learn more about the role and qualifications. Then take the next step toward a career with purpose, measurable results, and lasting significance. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants are encouraged to apply by August 31, 2026, for best consideration. Appointment Date: Start date will be determined after acceptance of an offer and background check clearance. Required Application Details We will require application materials to include a completed application , a cover letter introducing the candidate and highlighting their interest in the position, their qualifications, and an explanation as to why they are a good fit for the role and the organization, as well as a resume. References are not required at this time, but may be requested from candidates as the search progresses. Material should be submitted as one PDF to FoundationHR@fhsu.edu . Questions If you have questions regarding this role, please contact Laura Dougherty at ladougherty@fhsu.edu . *Review of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Because of the sensitive nature of FHSU Foundation business and the importance of our reputation with donors, the FHSU Foundation conducts a comprehensive review of all applicants. By submitting your application, you authorize us to conduct reference checks and a review of available public information. Employment is contingent upon background and reference checks that the FHSU Foundation finds acceptable.* Why Join the Fort Hays State University Foundation? You'll join a team that’s ambitious and committed to a shared goal of creating opportunities for students and strengthening one of Kansas' leading regional universities. We believe great employees deserve exceptional support. At the FHSU Foundation, we invest in our employees as much as our mission. We strive to build upon your strengths, provide options for professional growth, and foster a collaborative, welcoming workplace where everyone can contribute and thrive. That’s why we offer an outstanding benefits package and unique perks that set us apart: Competitive, market-leading compensation Company-paid health, dental, vision, and life insurance A 401(k) with an immediate 10% employer contribution Generous paid time off, wellness leave, holidays, and reduced summer hours Tuition assistance, professional development, and certification support An engaging workplace culture focused on collaboration, innovation, and employee engagement About Us The FHSU Foundation is an independent 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization that advances Fort Hays State University through private philanthropy. Since 1945, we've partnered with alumni, donors, corporations, and friends of the university to create scholarships, enhance academic programs, and expand opportunities that transform the lives of our students. FHSU Home FHSU Alumni Employee Access Board Access Campus Forms Tax ID: 48-6108086 Ways To Give I Fed The Tiger Annual Giving Leadership Giving Legacy Giving Impact Student Stories Donor Impact About News Staff Contact Board of Trustees Privacy Policy Financials Careers FAQ Make A Gift Fort Hays State University Foundation One Tiger Place, Hays, Kansas 67601 | 785-628-5620 Follow Follow Follow Follow"
    },
    "https://acesrch.applicantstack.com/x/detail/a21esjy12xzt": {
      "title": "Fort Hays State University - Chair, Department of Management - Academic Career & Executive Search",
      "description": "Fort Hays State University - Chair, Department of Management - Academic Career & Executive Search My Account Job Openings >> Fort Hays State University - Chair, Department of Management Fort Hays State University - Chair, Department of Management Summary Title: Fort Hays State University - Chair, Department of Management ID: 1427 More about this job > Description Fort Hays State University Chair, Department of Management Academic Career & Executive Search is pleased to assist Fort Hays State University in its search for Chair, Department of Management. A central component of the Robbins College of Business & Entrepreneurship (RCOBE), the Department of Management (the Department) at Fort Hays State University (FHSU) is well positioned for its next chapter of leadership and growth. Supported by experienced faculty, established academic programs, and a broad portfolio of disciplines, the next Chair will work with faculty and college leadership to advance curricular innovation, strengthen connections with employers and industry partners, and ensure students are prepared for success in a changing business environment. Recognized as one of the Midwest's most innovative regional universities, FHSU serves more than 12,000 students through its residential campus, online programs, and international partnerships. The University continues to expand its impact through workforce partnerships, new academic pathways, and its Strategic Affiliation Initiative connecting institutions and communities across Kansas and beyond. The Department of Management plays an important role in supporting these efforts through business education, workforce preparation, and community engagement. The Department delivers undergraduate and graduate programs, supports core BBA and MBA curricula, and prepares students to lead in an increasingly complex business environment. Through on-campus, online, and global partnership programs, the Department advances the University's mission while extending its reach across Kansas, the nation, and internationally. Academic strengths span management, human resource management, entrepreneurship, business law, and related disciplines. The Chair provides strategic, academic, and operational leadership for the department. The Chair will foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, student success, and continuous improvement while building consensus around shared priorities, supporting faculty development, strengthening external partnerships, and ensuring programs remain responsive to evolving workforce and educational needs. The position is a 12-month, tenure-track appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor rank and reports to the Dean of the College. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The Chair provides academic, administrative, and operational leadership for the Department of Management and is responsible for the overall management and success of the department. Key responsibilities include: Managing the department budget and other financial resources. Overseeing course scheduling, curriculum management, and academic program quality. Initiating and facilitating high-quality academic programs, certificates, partnerships, and other on-campus and online educational opportunities. Leading annual program assessment activities and supporting continuous improvement efforts. Conducting goal setting and performance reviews for faculty and staff. Leading student recruitment and retention initiatives within the department. Promoting collegiality and collaboration within the department, college, and university. Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses through on-campus and online modalities. Ensuring departmental initiatives align with College, University, and Kansas Board of Regents strategic priorities. Participating in college and university service activities and maintaining an appropriate record of scholarly activity. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Earned doctorate from a regionally accredited institution in management, human resource management, entrepreneurship, production/operations management, business law, or a closely related discipline represented within the department. Demonstrated excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service sufficient to merit appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor at Fort Hays State University. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Record of successful academic administrative experience, including both fiscal and supervisory responsibilities. Demonstrated success with student recruitment and retention initiatives. Experience with formalized assessment processes. Record of external funding through grants and/or fundraising. Demonstrated success with online education. Experience developing and sustaining external partnerships. Experience with strategic planning and new program development. Benefits : To review FHSU's competitive benefits package, please visit FHSU Benefits . About Fort Hays State University Founded in 1902 as the Western Branch of Kansas State Normal School, Fort Hays State University (FHSU) is a comprehensive public university and a recognized leader in accessible, innovative higher education. Serving more than 12,000 students from Kansas, across the United States, and around the world, FHSU offers more than 200 academic programs spanning business, education, health and behavioral sciences, arts and humanities, science and mathematics, and applied technology. Located in Hays, Kansas, FHSU combines the personalized attention of a regional institution with a global reach. Through its residential campus, FHSU Online, and an extensive network of international partnership campuses, the university delivers affordable, high-quality educational opportunities to diverse learners, including traditional students, working professionals, military-affiliated students, and international populations. This distinctive model has positioned FHSU as a national leader in distance and international education while maintaining a strong commitment to student success and academic excellence. Guided by its mission to provide accessible, affordable, and high-quality education, Fort Hays State University continues to expand its impact as a forward-thinking institution that advances economic development, workforce preparation, and educational opportunity throughout Kansas and beyond. Learn more about the university here: Quick Facts About the Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship and the Department of Management The W.R. and Yvonne Robbins College of Business and Entrepreneurship ( RCOBE ) prepares future business leaders through innovative, student-centered education emphasizing entrepreneurship, applied learning, and professional engagement. More than 50 full-time faculty, 50 adjunct faculty, and 10 professional and support staff serve approximately 1,700 domestic undergraduate students, 260 domestic graduate students, and 1,400 international students through campus, online, and international partnership programs. Guided by the university's \"Forward Thinking. World Ready.\" philosophy, the College equips graduates with the knowledge, skills, and leadership capabilities necessary to succeed in a dynamic global economy. One of four academic departments within the College, the Department of Management plays a vital role in delivering undergraduate and graduate business education. The department offers degree programs and certificates through on-campus, online, and global partnership pathways while also supporting core BBA and MBA curricula. Faculty combine academic expertise and professional experience to prepare students to think strategically, lead effectively, and succeed in a dynamic business environment. The department is committed to innovation, workforce relevance, and continuous improvement and is well-positioned to expand its impact through curricular innovation, industry engagement, student success initiatives, and new program development. Living in the Area Located in the heart of western Kansas, Hays offers an exceptional quality of life with affordable housing, short commute times, excellent healthcare, and a powerful sense of community. Home to approximately 20,000 residents, Hays serves as the region's economic, educational, healthcare, and cultural hub, providing many of the amenities of a larger city while maintaining the accessibility and friendliness of a close-knit community. Residents enjoy a cost of living well below the national average, highly regarded schools, diverse dining and shopping options, and abundant recreational opportunities. The community features an extensive network of parks, trails, athletic facilities, golf courses, and aquatic amenities, while nearby lakes, state parks, and wildlife areas offer opportunities for boating, fishing, camping, hunting, and outdoor recreation. Hays Regional Airport offers daily commercial air service, and the community is conveniently located along Interstate 70, providing easy access to destinations throughout Kansas and the Midwest. Learn more about the area here: Visit Hays To Apply Please apply through the application link and do not email applications. Applications will be reviewed as they are received and should include a cover letter and curriculum vita. Ideally cover letters should not exceed two pages. All applications are treated confidentially. Inquiries, referrals, and nominations are also treated confidentially. Inquiries and questions: Please send to FHSUChairMgt@acesrch.com Nominations and referrals: Please send the nominee’s name, title, and contact information if available to nominations@acesrch.com . Institutional Information Notice of Non-discrimination: FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. Background Check: Final candidate will have consented to and successfully completed a criminal background check. Notice to KPERS retirees applying for a position: Recent legislation changes working-after-retirement rules for both you and your employer if you go back to work for a KPERS employer. Please contact your KPERS representative or www.kpers.org for further information on how this might affect you. Apply Now Refer to a Friend Alternatively, you can apply to this job using your profile from Indeed by clicking the button below: Copyright 2026 Academic Career & Executive Search. All rights reserved. Powered by ApplicantStack™ Hiring Automation Software Privacy Policy | Terms of Use"
    },
    "https://www.academicsearch.org/open-searches-public/entry/25893/?search=25893": {
      "title": "Open Searches",
      "description": "Current Open Searches Join Our Network Inquire About Our Services Portal Login About Us Mission Values Work with Leadership Development Organizations Board of Directors Our Services Executive Search Executive Coaching Transition and Onboarding Our Team Open Searches Our Results Featured Appointments Past Partnerships Resources and News Podcasts Resources Contact Us Menu Menu Open Searches Academic Search specializes in executive searches for colleges, universities, and related organizations—partnering with institutions to assemble the strongest teams possible. We recognize that recruiting strong leaders is crucial to the success of any higher education institution and it is our goal to find the right candidate for each role. We are committed to building exceptional and deep pools of candidates for all searches, and we encourage you to look through our open searches to learn more about the opportunities available at our partner institutions. Dean of the College of Health and Behavioral Sciences Download Profile Application deadline: October 20, 2026 APPLY Senior Consultant: Cynthia Patterson Cynthia.Patterson@academicsearch.org Search Manager: Penny Gibbons Penny.Gibbons@academicsearch.org Fort Hays State University (FHSU) invites inquiries, applications, and nominations for the position of Dean of the College of Health and Behavioral Sciences (CHBS). The successful candidate will be an administrative leader, collaborator, visionary, communicator, and successful teacher-scholar who respects the culture and history of this student-centered institution and who understands great teaching and advising, the role of research in student learning, and the value of professional service. The Dean will work with the Provost and Academic Affairs team to advance both the College and the University in alignment with the Academic Affairs Priorities and University Strategic Plan . The next Dean will advocate for faculty and staff, demonstrate accountability, and balance quantitative data with human-centered judgment to inform decisions and measure success. The Dean serves on the Academic Council and Strategy Teams, the President’s Cabinet, the Senior Leadership Team, and other university-level administrative and planning groups. The appointment is a 12-month academic administrative position reporting to the Provost/Vice President for Academic Affairs. FHSU offers a competitive benefit package . The earliest start date is January 2027, with flexibility to begin as late as July 1, 2027. Founded in 1902, FHSU is a forward-thinking Midwest university enrolling more than 15,500 students: 4,500+ on the Hays campus, 4,000 through its China partnership program, and over 7,000 online. More than 400 faculty and 500 professional staff members support certificate, associate’s, bachelor’s, and master’s programs, as well as the Doctor of Nursing Practice, across 31 departments in five colleges and the Graduate School. The College of Health and Behavioral Sciences is dedicated to advancing the health and well-being of individuals and communities through innovative education, research, and service. Its programs cultivate a diverse, inclusive learning environment that fosters academic excellence, ethical leadership, and professional growth. Serving more than 3,000 undergraduate and graduate students, the College offers degree programs in allied health , communication sciences and disorders , health and human performance , nursing , psychology and social work . Programs are delivered on campus, online, and through international partnerships. The CHBS is also home to the Herndon Speech Language Clinic, Psychology Testing Clinic, and the Senior Companion/Foster Grandparents Program. Academic Search is partnering with Fort Hays State University on this search, which is led by Dr. Cynthia Patterson, Managing Director. All inquiries, applications, and nominations will be held in confidence . For more information about the position, institution, qualifications and online application process, please review the full position profile on the Academic Search website: https://www.academicsearch.org/open-searches-public/ . Candidates are welcome to send a CV to FHSUDeanCHBS@academicsearch.org to schedule a confidential conversation. Please do not send application materials by email . For full consideration by the Search Committee, candidates should submit all application materials by Tuesday, October 20, 2026. Nominations are not required, but leaders who know of outstanding candidates are welcome to submit confidential nominations to FHSUDeanCHBS@academicsearch.org . Please include the nominee’s full name, position, institution or organization, and email address. FHSU is committed to providing equal opportunity and access to its educational programs, employment, services, and activities in compliance with federal and state nondiscrimination laws. FHSU prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation on the basis of race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, and gender identity and expression), age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in its programs, activities, admissions, or employment. APPLY 1250 Connecticut Avenue NW, Suite 700 PMB 5334 Washington, DC 20036-2657 Phone: 202-332-4049 Fax: 202-234- 7640 LinkedIn Podcast ©2026 Academic Search Confidentiality Policy Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Policy Social Media Policy Privacy Policy Scroll to top Scroll to top Scroll to top"
    },
    "https://www.fhsu.edu/career/index": {
      "title": "Cookies on this site",
      "description": "Career Development Skip to main content Cookies on this site We use cookie to improve your experience and analyze site traffice. Learn morw Accept Reject Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Visit Give Directory News About Academics Admissions Athletics International Online Apply Career Development Home Career Development Closer to the Job of Your Dreams Your college experience ultimately helps illuminate the path toward the job of your dreams and the career of a lifetime. Fort Hays State University past and present students alike have utilized our offered resources and network of connections to get ahead – and stay there. Advance Your Future Get Ready, Get Set Stay ahead of the work – and the competition – by preparing yourself with the necessary knowledge and tools that will help you excel. Resume & Cover Letter Assistance - Write a resume and cover letter with the help of Career Development to help you land the job interview that sets you up for your future. Interviewing - Develop your interview skills through mock interviews, our online video interview training software Big Interview , and sample interview questions so your practice can make perfect when the right opportunity comes. Networking - Create lines of communication within the job market and build a network of professionals who understand your search. Job Search Booklet – You don’t have to search alone. Take information with you on how best to dress, search for jobs, maintain a personal calendar, and get ahead in finding the right job. Events - Enhance your career readiness by attending career fairs and other events. Graduate School Resources - Thinking about graduate school? Learn more about writing personal statements and admissions information. Tailored for Tigers – This professional clothing closet is free of change to currently enrolled FHSU students who want to dress to impress for interviews, business presentations, career fairs, or other professional activities. Find an Internship or Job Fort Hays State University is here to help get you ready not only to graduate, but to pursue the career of your choice. Whether you are still registered and looking for an internship or part-time job or getting ready to graduate and pursue career opportunities, our vacancy listings can help you get ahead. Handshake - Explore full-time job and internship listings, resume referrals, alumni networking and on-campus interviewing opportunities. GoinGlobal – Get information for students and alumni looking to job search globally and internationally. Internships – Apply your classroom learning, explore career options, and gain relevant work experience through internship opportunities. Career Fairs - Meet a large variety of potential employers under one roof with information on potential jobs and internship opportunities. Menu Career Development About Us Students Undergraduate Students Online Students International Students Veteran Students Graduate Students Video Presentations Employers Post a Job/Internship Career Fairs On-Campus Recruiting On-Campus Internships Faculty Calendar of Events Handshake Student/Alumni Login Employer Login About Handshake Tailored for Tigers Career Exploration Overview Current Students Prospective Students What Can I Do With A Major In... Majors and Graduate Programs Fair Staff How to Reach Us Career Development Fort Hays State University 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601 Center for Student Success 142 Phone: 785-628-4260 Email: careers@fhsu.edu Hours: Monday - Friday: 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Online Careers Apply Request Info Visit Give Help & Concerns Accessibility Ideas to Improve Freedom of Expression 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601-4099 785-628-FHSU (3478) © 2026 Fort Hays State University. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.fhsu.edu/career/jft/index": {
      "title": "Cookies on this site",
      "description": "Jobs for Tigers Skip to main content Cookies on this site We use cookie to improve your experience and analyze site traffice. Learn morw Accept Reject Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Visit Give Directory News About Academics Admissions Athletics International Online Apply Jobs for Tigers Home Career Development Jobs for Tigers Part-time Jobs for Tigers Looking for a part-time, off-campus job while going to school? If so, check out Handshake and get help locating part-time and temporary employment in the Hays area. Login to your Handshake account with your Workday username and password. Once logged in, go to Jobs on the menu bar. Select Part-Time Job and type Hays, KS . If you would like to receive emails when new jobs are posted, you will need to create a search alert in Handshake. Creating a search alert is easy, just select the link on the right side of the Jobs page. Career Development has partnered with Handshake - a modern career development platform - to be your one-stop-shop for finding part-time jobs in the Hays area, as well as nationwide full-time and internship opportunities. As of May 14, 2018, part-time off campus Jobs for Tigers listings are posted through Handshake. *Handshake does not list jobs that are on-campus.* Please contact the Student Employment office, Picken Hall Room 207A to inquire about on-campus jobs. Fort Hays State University makes no representations or guarantees about positions listed by the Career Development office. FHSU is not responsible for safety, wages, working conditions, or other aspects of off-campus employment. It is the responsibility of the student to research the integrity of the organizations to which they are applying for any position with an organization or private party. Menu Career Development About Us Students Undergraduate Students Online Students International Students Veteran Students Graduate Students Video Presentations Employers Post a Job/Internship Career Fairs On-Campus Recruiting On-Campus Internships Faculty Calendar of Events Handshake Student/Alumni Login Employer Login About Handshake Tailored for Tigers Career Exploration Overview Current Students Prospective Students What Can I Do With A Major In... Majors and Graduate Programs Fair Staff How to Reach Us Career Development Fort Hays State University 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601 Center for Student Success 142 Phone: 785-628-4260 Email: careers@fhsu.edu Hours: Monday - Friday: 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Online Careers Apply Request Info Visit Give Help & Concerns Accessibility Ideas to Improve Freedom of Expression 600 Park Street Hays, KS 67601-4099 785-628-FHSU (3478) © 2026 Fort Hays State University. All rights reserved."
